/// known-gap: interp has no overlay classes (`<^>`); the interpreter is being retired
/// An overlay is an object: `:objects(Government)` gives the overlays of
/// an overlay class, declared or made while the program runs, in the
/// order they were made, each with its `overlay_name`, `parents`, the
/// `intensity` a new copy starts at and its fields (a member takes the
/// class's fields it doesn't write). A condition picks among them.
<>Realm |
    rank: 1
xx
<^>Government |
    hosts: Realm
    dup: replace
    rule: "none"
    term: 4
xx
overlay chiefdom <^> Government
    rule: "chief"
xx
overlay council <^> Government
    term: 10
xx
repeat :objects(Government) as g
    :say("{g >> overlay_name}: rule {g >> rule}, term {g >> term}, parents {g >> parents}")
xx
:say(:len(:objects(Government, it >> term > 5)))
act found(r)
    overlay junta <^> Government
        rule: "army"
    xx
    :overlay!(r, junta)
xx
r <> Realm | rank: 1
found(r)
found(r)
repeat :objects(Government, it >> rule == "army") as g
    :say(g >> overlay_name)
xx
